4) APPLICATION FRAMEWORK AND LIBRARIES

   Rust crates and npm packages are resolved at build time and are not vendored here.
   The direct dependencies are declared in src-tauri/Cargo.toml and package.json, and
   the exact resolved versions in src-tauri/Cargo.lock and package-lock.json.

   The principal ones: Tauri (MIT OR Apache-2.0), rusqlite with bundled SQLite
   (MIT; SQLite itself is public domain), React (MIT), zustand (MIT),
   html-to-image (MIT), image (MIT OR Apache-2.0), msedge-tts (MIT),
   rustls (Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT), ureq (MIT OR Apache-2.0),
   zip (MIT), sha2 (MIT OR Apache-2.0), quick-xml (MIT), serde (MIT OR Apache-2.0).

   All are permissive. Each remains under the terms granted by its own copyright holder,
   and those terms continue to apply to those components.

